  "interpretation": [
    "The DAPO training parquet contains exact or layout-only matches for 13 of the 902 evaluation problems, concentrated in AMC23 and MATH500; the formal six-benchmark result must disclose this limitation.",
    "Removing all 13 layout-normalized exact overlaps leaves a positive macro delta with a strictly positive problem-bootstrap interval, so known exact overlap does not explain the I8 seed-42 gain.",
    "The word 5-gram rule flags 29 problems but misses one layout-normalized exact match, so the most conservative sensitivity excludes their 30-problem union; the positive macro delta and strictly positive interval remain.",
    "Only one of the 13 exact-overlap evaluation problems was actually consumed in the seed-42 50-step data order, and all seed-42 methods consumed the same 3200 prompts.",
    "None of the 112 disjoint P2 source prompt UUIDs used across discovery, calibration, and audit matches the exact, lexical, or conservative-union evaluation sets.",
    "This post-hoc sensitivity does not alter the preregistered selector, does not establish semantic decontamination, and cannot replace training seeds 43 and 44."
